The first implementation passes G1–G8, but I found one important calibration issue before accepting it: the random-guess gate was sampling the full \((n!)^2\) format space. Because a chosen A–B pair uniquely determines its only locally feasible C value, that overstates hardness. I’m tightening G4 to sample locally compatible A–B assignments and only leave the global “all C values distinct” obstruction unresolved.
